Package: scoreAuditR
Type: Package
Title: Audit Scores and Predictions under Structured Missingness
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Dimas Novian Aditia", "Syahputra", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "maintainer@example.org")
Description: Reproducible sensitivity audits for repeated ordinal measurements
    and numeric country-year panels. Simulates graded response data, masks items
    under MCAR or observed-covariate MAR designs, and evaluates mean, item-mode
    and known-calibration expected a posteriori scores and changes.
    Imports World Happiness Report CSV files, separates country or time partitions,
    masks observed predictors with explicit pattern geometry, fits training-only
    imputation and ridge regression, and compares prediction and exact linear
    interventional Shapley attribution stability against a matched reference.
    Provides simulated examples, export utilities and an optional Shiny interface.
    Not a psychometric validation or causal inference tool.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, utils, tools
Suggests: shiny
NeedsCompilation: no
URL: https://github.com/dimasnovian/scoreAuditR
